Package: PASSAGE
Type: Package
Title: Pathway-Level Spatial Association Testing
Version: 0.6.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Diptavo", "Dutta", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "dutta.diptavo@gmail.com")
  )
Author: Diptavo Dutta
Maintainer: Diptavo Dutta <dutta.diptavo@gmail.com>
Description: Tests whether predefined gene sets show spatially varying
    expression after adjustment for measured covariates and background spatial
    structure. Implements sparse spatial factor models, self-contained and
    competitive pathway tests, pathway-level spatial effect-size and coherence
    metrics, and stability-based driver-gene analyses. Includes pathway-only
    component estimation, fixed-kernel subspace tests, and fitted Gaussian
    process covariance comparisons with conditional rotation calibration.
    Separates statistic construction from matched-set competitive calibration,
    including shared-background Cauchy, minimum-p and Fisher combinations.
    Provides pathway-local competitive statistics, conditional full-universe
    gene-set randomization, negative-control nuisance adjustment and an
    approximate residual wild-bootstrap option for unequal spot noise.
